WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:07.310
So yesterday, a day before presiding over
a joint session of Congress to confirm the

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:14.370
victory of Joe Biden as the next president
of the United States, Joe Biden, Mike Pence,

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:20.580
rather, Vice Vice President Mike Pence met
with Donald Trump and reportedly told him,

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.670
I can't overturn the election results.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:28.740
Donald Trump has been increasingly pointing
to Mike Pence, saying, we've got to count

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:29.740
on Mike Pence.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:31.480
Mike Pence has to come through for us.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:36.000
And that's code for figure out a way to steal
an election that we actually didn't win.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.060
And The New York Times is now reporting that
Mike Pence, quote, tried to lower the president's

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:45.740
expectations while seeking ways to mollify
him.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:50.350
This is an article by Anthony Carney and Maggie
Haberman where they say Vice President Mike

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:56.600
Pence told Trump on Tuesday that he didn't
believe he had the power to block congressional

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:02.050
certification of Joe Biden's win in the presidential
election, which is true, he doesn't.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:08.070
Despite Trump's baseless insistence that he
did and this is according to multiple people

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:10.480
briefed on the content of the conversation.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:15.740
This took place during the weekly lunch that
Mike Pence has with Donald Trump.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:23.480
And this was just hours after Trump started
publicly pressuring Mike Pence to essentially

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:25.070
steal the election for him.

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:29.740
I mean, we have to call things what they are
and these euphemisms about making sure all

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.200
legal votes are counted.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.060
We have the election results in every state.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.640
Those results have been certified.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.990
The electors have been certified their votes.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:42.450
And today and it may be happening as we speak,
it may be done by the time you listen to today's

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.720
show or watch this clip.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:49.990
The joint session of the House and Senate
is counting those votes.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:54.560
Trump tweeted, The president has the power
to reject fraudulently chosen electors.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:59.700
And, of course, it is not true that there
were fraudulently chosen electors.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.560
None of this is true.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:07.049
And most importantly, Mike Pence cannot alter
the results.

00:02:07.049 --> 00:02:12.140
Mike Pence can hear objections from senators
and members of the House, which we expect

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:13.250
to hear.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.140
There can be debate about that.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:24.000
We heard that Tim Scott and James Inhofe to
radical right senators are saying that they

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.080
will not be participating in these attempts
to undermine the results.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:32.599
But reportedly 11 or 12 Republican senators
are going to.

00:02:32.599 --> 00:02:35.310
So there's a few different aspects to this.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:39.240
Number one, January 20th really couldn't get
here any faster.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:43.300
We're down to exactly two weeks, two weeks
to the day.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:47.510
Joe Biden will be getting sworn in and Trump
will be we don't know where.

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:50.010
